  "limits": [
    "Separate explicit profile of existing local owner policy. Zero-age product and fixture defaults remain fresh-only; no production runtime behavior changed.",
    "Each worker retains its own bounded private cache across generations. Reused receipts retain supporting observation age and cached-target-readback level; they do not guarantee current persistence.",
    "New parts and descriptors remain verified. The unchanged phase performed zero GETs of retained parts. Subsequent adapter materialization and all seven independent old-reader/oracle recoveries read actual bytes with no cache mounted.",
    "The fresh-only control remains accepted on its exact source; the delay-only WebDAV concurrency failure, canonical-input rejection, temporary-root refusal and earlier short-deadline failures are not relabelled.",
    "These cohosted 128 MiB measurements have different host/cache conditions; timings describe these runs and do not establish a speedup guarantee or a 100 GiB bound.",
    "Memory-limit events indicate pressure. No RAM headroom, physical failure-domain, full-scale, real-account, asymmetric ingress or overall-product acceptance is claimed.",
    "Response-body counts exclude TCP/TLS framing. Parent checks and later independent downloads are recorded separately. Full profile admission still requires a terminal accepted physical source, exact committed CI and fresh resource/cost review."
  ],
